{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q5643464","formula":"C₉H₁₃NO","hill":"C9H13NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":13.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Halostachine"},"descriptions":{"en":"Halostachine (also known as N-methylphenylethanolamine) is a natural product, an alkaloid first isolated from the Asian shrub Halostachys caspica (synonym Halostachys belangeriana), and structurally a β-hydroxy-phenethylamine (a phenylethanolamine) related to its better-known \"parent\" biogenic amine, phenylethanolamine, to the adrenergic drug synephrine, and to the alkaloid ephedrine. The pharmacological properties of halostachine have some similarity to those of these structurally-related compounds, and Halostachys caspica extracts have been included as a constituent of certain OTC dietary supplements, but halostachine has never been developed as a prescription drug."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":6950649,"mass":151.21,"charge":0,"smiles":"CNC[C@@H](C1=CC=CC=C1)O","inchikey":"ZCTYHONEGJTYQV-VIFPVBQESA-N","iupac":"(1R)-2-(methylamino)-1-phenylethanol","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"6950649","atoms":24,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.139,"y":1.668,"z":-0.824,"el":"O"},{"x":3.246,"y":-0.161,"z":-0.105,"el":"N"},{"x":0.874,"y":0.264,"z":-0.706,"el":"C"},{"x":1.857,"y":-0.362,"z":0.303,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.549,"y":0.07,"z":-0.302,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.246,"y":-1.062,"z":-0.726,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.182,"y":1.019,"z":0.501,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.576,"y":-1.243,"z":-0.347,"el":"C"},{"x":-2.512,"y":0.837,"z":0.879,"el":"C"},{"x":4.159,"y":-0.736,"z":0.872,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.209,"y":-0.294,"z":0.455,"el":"C"},{"x":1.044,"y":-0.168,"z":-1.7,"el":"H"},{"x":1.647,"y":-1.435,"z":0.399,"el":"H"},{"x":1.703,"y":0.099,"z":1.288,"el":"H"},{"x":3.431,"y":0.837,"z":-0.198,"el":"H"},{